00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
if you've been intimidated by arma in  the past or have fallen off the game  armor of forger now going into early  access is looking to hook you back in  with a smaller stand-alone experience  that the community can mod test and  change let's look at the good the bad  and if this game can capture a new  generation of arma players ahead of arma  4. arma led the way on military  simulation games for a long time with  countless scenarios great combined armed  big team battles and fantastic mods like  daisy that eventually evolved into games  like playerunknown's battlegrounds but  being very simulation based it was  always a game that was pretty tough for  general audiences to get into in more  recent times arm has seen pressure from  a host of other male sim titles like  squad insurgency sandstorm hell let  loose and rising storm just to name a  few those games tend to deliver a much  more honed experience that's far easier  to get into so is it time for a modern  arma game for a modern audience arma has  tried to slim down in the past he tried  project argo and now armorer forger is  looking to try again so there's good  news and bad news here the good news is  that armor or forger is a test bed for  arma 4. but the bad news is that arma 4  is still a ways off and not the army  game you'll get to play now in early  access armor or forger is a standalone  title that takes place on the island of  evron set in the 1980s but the location  is inspired by the former sovereign  state of czechoslovakia armor of forger  is releasing on both xbox and pc so mods  on pc will now work on xbox it's a game  that's looking to be a place for the  arma community to put the new infusion  engine to the test and hopefully work  out the kinks and bugs ahead of arma 4.  there are two multiplayer game modes  conflict and game master in conflict you  capture positions around the map and in  game master players take on more  specific combat scenarios and those can  be edited on the fly there's also a  workshop for people to start modding and  developing their own ideas so who is  arma reforger for i'm coming at this as  a battlefield and call of duty player  who's dabbled in milsim titles like  insurgency and rising storm but also  play games with massive player counts  like mag and planetside 2. arma is still  for people who really like hardcore  military simulation games that hasn't  really changed i mean it this is beyond  just needing a mic and a few friends  this is needing a large organized crew  of players as we experience playing a  few hours of conflict my first few  rounds were really just stumbling around  learning to navigate with a compass and  a map again then sorting out who i was  supposed to be shooting at and then  getting killed by things in the distance  which is very arma it took a while to  get acclimated to the game but again if  you're an avid arma player that probably  won't be too difficult for you for  better or worse like all games you play  with friends a lot of the fun comes down  to who you play with all right  once an experienced group jumped on the  server it was a whole different game it  had a pretty good time this group was  extremely organized like commanders  would go off to the side and hash out a  plan then team leaders wrangled us up  into squads and navigated us to  objectives if it went bad there was a  person back at headquarters who  organized respawning players back into  squads and sent them back out again with  more orders and that level of  coordination has always been the thing  that both makes arma like nothing else  and also a huge barrier for people who  are just trying to play or just trying  to learn and also a huge barrier that  can hold the game back moving forward  for a larger more mainstream audience  when it comes together there are amazing  moments where planning pays off and  everything just falls into place the  combat and arma yeah it's fun as hell  patrolling a road and getting into  contact or fending off waves of  counter-attacks or just the sheer volume  of outbound fire at times is truly  something  at one point my squad was killed right  next to me and i didn't even know they  were dead because it was night and their  comms just went silent then suddenly i  was surrounded by enemy forces who were  about as surprised as i was arma does a  great job of simulating that chaos  confusion and even boredom of war you'll  spend a lot of time just either standing  around and planning or traveling to  places with brief thrilling firefights  at the end you have to be okay with that  slower pace but there's a satisfaction  in the tension and the build up to these  moments where hopefully your planning  paid off it makes you realize the  constant action in games like call of  duty can feel hollow and kind of  pointless at times so if armor or forger  is so reliant on group play but wants to  pull in a larger audience and maybe pull  in those laps battlefield players it  might need to start adding more modern  conveniences like waypoint markers  contextual call out and ping systems and  a commander system that doesn't need  squads to physically talk to each other  that could massively lower the barrier  to entry i'm thinking about say the ping  system from apex the commander system  from battlefield 4 and just kind of like  all of what planetside 2 does it's hard  to see if armor or forger doesn't have  these things because they haven't been  put in it's early access or they're  there but buried in menus or the game  just trying to be authentic to an 80s  setting again we only spent a couple  hours with it and because of the mod  ability we might see these things appear  as time goes on but if you're used to  these modern gaming comforts this might  not be the title for you  another thing that's kind of always been  in arma is that simple actions are just  still somehow overly complicated in a  way that isn't the case in so many other  titles people struggle to figure out how  to spawn vehicles from menus start up a  humvee and drive it save a loadout and  figure out where to join a squad that  was buried a few menus deep again that  being said more veteran arma players on  our server were saying that they were  pleased with some of the quality of life  improvements so it does seem better if  you're familiar with the series already  another thing and i say this is someone  coming at the game who's played armor in  the past and also played games like pubg  but the grid inventory system just feels  outdated in a way that pulls you out of  the experience every time you have to  use it many modern games have simplified  these systems with classes or loadouts  or only needing to go into your  inventory for some things some of these  older design choices could make it less  likely that newcomers will stick around  when it comes to weapons the 80s theme  keeps things simple you won't find a lot  or any attachments so far and most  weapons only sport iron sights  fortunately arma does have a clever  trick which is when you long click the  mouse you can focus in on targets almost  like you have binoculars attached to  your eyes and if you then fast click the  mouse you'll transition to aiming down  sights that helps you see soldiers who  are far off which is usually the range  you'll be fighting at for those who want  an even closer look there was one  designated marksman rifle with a scope  that could be zeroed into different  ranges other than that weapons just  kinda were what they were you could grab  a variety of them from the base and head  out hoping you made the right choice  shooting feels very snappy and  controllable with the series usual  bullet physics and a lot of what you'd  be doing is suppressive fire anyway on  that note nothing grabs your attention  like that crack and whiz of enemy  bullets flying over your head as they  shoot back  when it came to the new game engine  itself i'm not an expert here but things  like lighting and water looked better to  my eyes the game was fairly stable  although still had plenty of glitches  like funky ground textures and sometimes  frame rate drops and let's just say that  nighttime was a little too  nighttime-ish like i get it night is  dark but from a gameplay perspective you  need to see what you're doing there are  compromises that can be made here my  squad stumbled around in the dark one  night for quite a while because while  you can turn on a flashlight and hold  the gun at the same time the flashlight  doesn't point in the same direction as  your weapon this is where modern  attachments and weapon lights can have a  positive impact on gameplay we didn't  have night vision goggles or anything  maybe that's something that could come  later when it came to the 80s theme some  things worked and some things didn't but  look that's the entire point of armor or  forger it's there to test and mod and  get the community involved in the  development of arma 4. so let us know  what you think of the comments below are  you a massive arma fan and see potential  here for a new generation of arma  players or are you someone who's never  played an army game before what would  get you into hardcore military sim  titles like this we cover a wide variety  of first person and third person  shooters so head on over to gamespot and  gamespot's youtube page heck we have a  modern warfare 2 coming up this year  thanks for watching

